# NetBeans Form Editor

When creating or editing `.form` screens in this project:

## Custom components need a no-arg constructor

NetBeans instantiates beans at design time via reflection. Any custom component used in a `.form` file must expose a public no-arg constructor, even when runtime code uses a parameterized constructor.

```java
/** No-arg constructor required by the NetBeans Form Editor at design time. */
public PlaceholderTextField() {
    this("Placeholder");
}
```

In the `.form` file, keep `JavaCodeGenerator_CreateCodeCustom` so generated `initComponents()` still uses the real placeholder text:

```xml
<AuxValue name="JavaCodeGenerator_CreateCodeCustom" type="java.lang.String"
          value="new PlaceholderTextField(&quot;Enter your email&quot;)"/>
```

Apply this pattern to all custom Swing beans: `PlaceholderTextField`, `PlaceholderPasswordField`, `GradientBackgroundPanel`, `LogoPanel`, `CardPanel`, etc.

## `.form` layout metadata must be complete

The Design tab reads layout from the `.form` file, not only from generated Java. Never leave empty layout stubs like:

```xml
<!-- BAD: Design tab cannot load this -->
<Layout class="org.netbeans.modules.form.compat2.layouts.DesignGroupLayout"/>
```

Always include full `DimensionLayout` blocks (dim `0` and `1`) that match the `GroupLayout` in `initComponents()`. Use `LoginFrame.form` or `SignUpFrame.form` as references.

## JScrollPane: design in Java, not in `.form`

The Form Editor cannot load `DesignScrollPaneLayout`. For scrollable screens:

- In `.form`: `pnlBackground` → `pnlScrollHost` (JPanel) → `pnlCard` with full `GroupLayout` metadata
- In `customizeForm()`: wrap `pnlScrollHost` in a `JScrollPane` (see `SignUpFrame.installScrollPane()`)

Do not place `JScrollPane` in the `.form` file.

## Screen structure pattern

- Put layout and component tree in `initComponents()` (generated from `.form`).
- Put fonts, colours, scroll-pane wiring, visibility toggles, and navigation in a private `customizeForm()` called after `initComponents()`.
- Do not hand-edit code inside `GEN-BEGIN` / `GEN-END` regions except through the Form Editor.
